 149: ## Dev Notes
 150: 
 151: ### Pre-story investigation (this session, read-only, no writes)
 152: 
 153: This is genuinely useful groundwork, not just epic-restatement — re-verify all of it at dev time
 154: rather than trusting it, since routes may have changed and this was a static read, not a live-data
 155: query:
 156: 
 157: - **`office_manoeuvre_ranks`**: `server/routes/office-manoeuvre-rank.js`'s two `PUT` routes both use
 158:   `upsert: true`, but only fire on an ST actively setting/stepping a rank — a seat nobody has touched
 159:   never gets a document. `server/routes/office-seats.js:501-544`'s `resetManoeuvreRank` (the
 160:   oxp-5 handover-reset path) explicitly uses `upsert: false` with an inline comment naming the exact
 161:   reasoning: *"A seat that never purchased a rank has no document, nothing to destroy, and needs no
 162:   document minted saying so... keeps the collection's 'no document = 0' convention intact."* This is
 163:   a **deliberate, already-documented, cross-file-consistent convention**, not an accident. `GET /`
 164:   does `for (const doc of docs) out[doc._id] = doc.rank || 0` — an absent collection simply produces
 165:   `{}`, and the client already treats a missing key as rank 0 (per the route's own comment).
 166: - **`office_merit_dots`**: same shape, same convention (`server/routes/office-merit-dots.js`'s own
 167:   `GET /` comment: *"a seat never purchased into yet simply has no key here — the client treats a
 168:   missing entry as 0 dots for every merit"*). 2 live documents means 2 real purchases have actually
 169:   happened at the table — this collection is not "empty by accident", it has real (if sparse) data.
 170: - **`office_actions`**: structurally different — an applied-action ledger
 171:   (`server/routes/office-actions.js`), not a current-state collection, gated behind `PAID_TYPES`/
 172:   `GATED_TYPES` and a separate pending-approval collection (`contested_roll_requests`, oaq-2/oaq-3).
 173:   `GET /` requires `game_session_id` and returns `[]` gracefully on no match. 0 live documents here is
 174:   a different kind of fact than the other two — it says "no office action has ever been approved
 175:   through this pipeline", which needs Task 2's own investigation to confirm is really "nothing has
 176:   happened yet" and not "something in the write path silently fails."
 177: - **The "renders differently against dev fixtures than production" claim (epic text) could not be
 178:   traced to a dev-fixtures interceptor entry** — none of the three collections' endpoints appear in
 179:   the fetch-interceptor pattern this project uses for local dev (see `reference_dev_fixtures` memory:
 180:   "patches fetch under local-test-token"), and no matches exist under `data/dev-fixtures/`. This needs
 181:   Task 3's own investigation (Playwright fixtures / local seed data are the likelier source) rather
 182:   than being taken as already-explained.
 183: - **The epic's "oxp-1 through oxp-7 done, not yet merged" premise is stale.** `git log origin/main`
 184:   (checked this session) shows `oxp-1`, `oxp-2`, `oxp-3`, `oxp-4`, `oxp-5` (PR #1165, merge commit
 185:   `1063787b`), `oxp-6`, and `oxp-11` are all already reachable from `origin/main` — this repo's own
 186:   `sprint-status.yaml` epic-oxp row (checked the same session) is itself stale on this point (claims
