 162: // transactional route that keeps the two in step atomically and leave every
 163: // existing read site alone. This is that route. Every other reader of
 164: // `court_category` is unchanged and stays correct.
 165: //
 166: // It also implements the handover half of content/rules/office-powers.md
 167: // (umbrella root, Angelus's ruling 2026-08-11): "Permanent merits stay when the
 168: // office changes hands... Manoeuvres reset to zero, and the XP spent on them is
 169: // lost. Not refunded, not banked, gone." `office_merit_dots` is therefore
 170: // touched NOWHERE in this file — merits persist by construction, because a
 171: // seat's `_id` never changes (oxp.11's core guarantee) — while
 172: // `office_manoeuvre_ranks` is reset below.
