 456: /**
 457:  * oxp.5 AC5 + AC6: zero this seat's manoeuvre rank and RECORD the XP that zeroing
 458:  * destroys. Called on every real handover, replacement and vacate alike.
 459:  *
 460:  * Vacating IS a handover. The ruling's wording is "on handover" / "when the
 461:  * office changes hands", and a departing holder's investment dies with their
 462:  * tenure whether or not a successor is named — the office-powers ruling's own
 463:  * consequence 2 ("a holder near the end of their tenure has no reason to buy
 464:  * manoeuvres") depends on this being true. Vacate is not reset-exempt.
 465:  *
 466:  * ═══ WHY THE DESTROYED-XP COUNTER EXISTS (oxp.5 Finding 1 — read this before
 467:  * changing anything here) ═══
 468:  *
 469:  * Office spend is DERIVED, never stored. `officeXpSpentForCategory` in
 470:  * public/js/data/office-xp.js (oxp.2) computes it as the sum of the seat's
 471:  * current merit dots plus its current manoeuvre `rank`. So the instant this
 472:  * function sets `rank` to 0, the derived spend DROPS by the old rank and the
 473:  * office's balance RISES by exactly the amount office-powers.md says must be
 474:  * destroyed. The obvious implementation delivers the precise OPPOSITE of the
 475:  * rule: a refund.
 476:  *
 477:  * The ruling anticipated it: "The running balance is total accrued since
 478:  * creation, minus everything ever spent, INCLUDING THE SPEND THAT HAS SINCE
 479:  * BEEN LOST." Lost spend cannot be recovered from current state after the fact
 480:  * — it is destroyed by definition, and nothing else in the system records the
 481:  * rank a seat used to have. This function is the only place the information
 482:  * exists, so it is captured HERE or it is gone forever.
 483:  *
 484:  * ═══ HANDED FORWARD, DELIBERATELY (oxp.6 / oxp.7) ═══
 485:  *
 486:  * oxp.5 STORES this counter and does not consume it. `officeXpSpentForCategory`
 487:  * MUST eventually add `manoeuvre_xp_destroyed` to its total, or every balance
 488:  * it renders over-reports by the destroyed amount — which IS the refund the
 489:  * ruling forbids. Nothing renders that number today (office-xp.js has no
 490:  * consumer yet), so nothing is wrong on screen, and wiring it here would
 491:  * rewrite oxp.2's AC8 from inside this story. Whoever builds the first real
 492:  * consumer owns that arithmetic. Recorded here, in oxp.5's Dev Notes and in
 493:  * oxp.6's sprint-status entry, the same way oxp.11 recorded `holder_id` into
 494:  * oxp.5 rather than leaving it to be rediscovered.
 495:  *
 496:  * @returns {Promise<{seat_id:string, rank_before:number, xp_destroyed:number,
 497:  *   manoeuvre_xp_destroyed_total:number}|null>} null when the seat has no rank
 498:  *   document at all (nothing was purchased, so nothing was destroyed).
 499:  */
 500: async function resetManoeuvreRank(seatId, category, timestamp, dbSession) {
 501:   const ranks = getCollection('office_manoeuvre_ranks');
 502:   // `findOneAndUpdate` rather than `updateOne`: it is the SAME single atomic
 503:   // aggregation-pipeline update (the same idiom office-manoeuvre-rank.js's step
 504:   // route uses), and it additionally hands back the pre-image, which is the only
 505:   // way to report the rank that was actually destroyed without adding a second
 506:   // read. A plain updateOne would leave the caller with `matchedCount` and no
 507:   // way to tell an ST what the operation cost them.
 508:   const result = await ranks.findOneAndUpdate(
 509:     { _id: seatId },
 510:     [
 511:       // STAGE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. Aggregation-pipeline stages run in
 512:       // sequence, so THIS stage reads the ORIGINAL `$rank` — before stage 2
 513:       // below zeroes it. Swap these two and the counter silently records 0
 514:       // destroyed on every handover, forever, with no error and no visible
 515:       // symptom until a balance is finally rendered. A test pins that exact
 516:       // inversion.
 517:       //
 518:       // The rate is 1 XP per rank (office-powers.md's flat "standard merit
 519:       // rate"), so the increment is exactly the pre-reset rank. The counter is
 520:       // CUMULATIVE across every handover this seat ever sees.
 521:       { $set: { manoeuvre_xp_destroyed: { $add: [{ $ifNull: ['$manoeuvre_xp_destroyed', 0] }, { $ifNull: ['$rank', 0] }] } } },
