2:# last_updated: "2026-08-14 (dbo-4 dev-storied to completion, all 6 tasks done, status ready-for-dev -> review. Read-only investigation, no code changed. AC1/AC2 confirmed NOT defects (both collections' 'no document = 0' convention is deliberate and consistent). AC3 - the story's one real finding - is URGENT and TIME-SENSITIVE: office_merit_dots holds 2 real, pre-oxp-11, category-keyed documents ('Enforcer'/'Head of State') invisible to the current seat-keyed code, because server/scripts/migrate-office-purchases-to-seats.mjs has never been run against live tm_suite. Confirmed via read-only live query plus a direct call to the migration's own pure planMigration() function (the CLI itself got blocked by the auto-mode permission classifier as live-DB-adjacent; worked around per its own suggestion by calling the exported function instead of shelling out - never --apply, never a write). Both docs currently hold only zeroes, so nothing of real value is at stake today, but the migration script's own header names a real compounding hazard if any ST touches either seat before it runs (creates a fresh seat-keyed doc, permanently orphaning the old one) - the window is open NOW since oxp-11 is already deployed. Running --apply is Angelus's own action, not flagged for execution here - see deferred-work.md's new entry and reference-data-ssot.md's new Office section. AC4: the epic's 'OXP not yet merged' premise was stale (oxp-1 through oxp-6 and oxp-11 all already merged) - epic-dbo-database-ownership.md and epic-oxp's own row both corrected. AC5: new Office (Court Positions) section added to reference-data-ssot.md. AC6: N/A, explicitly - no code defect found, nothing patched, nothing in server/ or public/ touched by this story. Full detail: dbo-4-office-collections-absent-empty-route.md's Dev Agent Record. Prior entry follows.)"
3:# last_updated_previously_dbo4: "2026-08-14 (dbo-4 story created (bmad-create-story). Pre-story investigation found the epic's own 'oxp not yet merged' premise is stale (oxp-1 through oxp-6 and oxp-11 already on origin/main; epic-oxp's own sprint-status row is stale on the same point) and that office_manoeuvre_ranks/office_merit_dots already follow a consistent, deliberately-documented 'no document = 0' convention across their writers - looks intentional, not a defect, but the story's own Tasks re-verify rather than trust this at dev time. office_actions (a different kind of collection, an applied-action ledger) still needs its own dedicated investigation. Story is investigation-first by design, mirroring DBO-1's own proven 'answer the question before writing code' shape - only Task 6 (fix a genuine defect, if Tasks 1-3 find one) writes code; Tasks 1-5 are read-only + documentation (specs/reference-data-ssot.md gets new entries for all three collections, satisfying the epic's own 'make it explicit rather than a discovery at the table' instruction). dbo-4 status: backlog -> ready-for-dev. epic-dbo still 2 of 9 done (dbo-1, dbo-3) - dbo-4 doesn't move that count until its own dev-story/review land. Full story: specs/stories/dbo-4-office-collections-absent-empty-route.md. Prior entry follows.)"
6:# last_updated_previously_2: "2026-08-14 (Epic DBO opened from a cross-app data audit run on the TM Wiki side; DBO-3 story created and ready-for-dev. Full context: D:\Terra Mortis\BRIEF-2026-08-14-tm-suite.md (the two rulings and the coordination protocol), specs/epic-dbo-database-ownership.md (all nine DBO stories), specs/deferred-work.md's own 'cross-app data audit' entry (the five Suite-side defects). Epic-dbo + all 9 story rows added to this file, all backlog except dbo-3. DBO-3 research found the epic's own naming (one call site) undersold the real bug: the SAME broken rule.sub_category==='standing' check is duplicated at three sites across two files (downtime-form.js, editor/merits.js x2), plus a fourth previously-unnamed defect where the sheet's own primary Add Merit picker has no standing-merit exclusion at all. Live-data query against tm_suite (read-only, no write) confirmed the epic's claim and the new finding precisely - full detail in dbo-3-xp-spend-standing-filter-bug.md's Dev Notes. Fix is a single shared predicate, isMeritEventGranted(rule), mirroring the shared-predicate-not-duplicated-logic pattern oxp-7's own AC2 just established. Branch hygiene: oxp-7 (fully reviewed, code-review closed, 77/77) was committed locally to its own branch ms/oxp-7-sheet-office-merits-section (NOT pushed, NOT merged - still held per the epic-oxp standing order) before starting this unrelated epic, so the two pieces of work do not share a branch. DBO-3 proceeds on a fresh ms/dbo-3-xp-spend-standing-filter-bug branch cut off main. Hard constraint carried from the brief: nothing from this repo deploys before the 2026-08-15 game; DBO-3's own fix is code-only, no tm_suite write, so it stays inside that freeze regardless of when dev-story runs. Prior entry follows.)" "2026-08-14 (oxp-5 code review via the codex-review skill, verify-before-accepting phase, picking up a prior session's mid-flight work: the codex prompt/diff/findings had already been generated and Codex's return had already landed (1 High, 7 Medium, 5 Low at specs/stories/code-review/oxp-5-codex-findings.md), and city-views.js/office-seats.js had already been partly patched, but the bookkeeping - story Status, Dev Agent Record, sprint-status, findings outcomes - had not been closed out, so this session verified every finding against the running code before trusting any of it (an unverified external review carries borrowed authority). Outcome: 1 High + 6 Medium patched, 3 Medium dismissed with evidence, 1 Medium informational, 1 Medium deferred, 2 Low patched, 1 Low deferred. Story status moved review -> done. NOT committed, NOT pushed, NOT merged - all of that remains Angelus's call. Full findings-by-finding outcome at specs/stories/code-review/oxp-5-codex-findings.md; full narrative at oxp-5-handover-logic.md's Senior Developer Review section. Prior entry follows.)" (1) Landed ms/oaq-3-docs-correction (PR #1149, merged to main bff75053, dev synced) fixing stale CSS/location notes left over from the same-day office-approvals game-app move. (2) Investigated TM Wiki's recent Ordeals work (Epic 30, all 5 stories, local-only on TM Wiki main, not deployed) for cross-project implications: confirmed Ordeals is NOT fully migrated - TM Wiki's new wiki_ordeal_submissions/wiki_player_prefs collections have no ingest path anywhere in TM Cockpit's grading pipeline, and TM Suite's own live Ordeals tab (admin domain 'ordeals', public/js/tabs/ordeals-view.js) is unaffected and still the only real authoring surface players can reach today. Left a handover doc in TM Cockpit (specs/cockpit/tm-wiki-ordeals-ingest-handover.md) for that repo's own session to build the ingest/marking skill TM Wiki's own scoping doc already named as Cockpit's job. Also surfaced, NOT YET FIXED: two real bugs in TM Suite's own live covenant-ordeal picker (public/js/tabs/covenant-data.js + ordeal-form.js) - the picked covenant is never actually persisted (covenant_choice lives outside the COVENANT_SECTIONS array collectResponses() walks), and every covenant reuses the same question keys (q2..q23) with no discriminator field, so a covenant change on a character could silently show stale cross-covenant answers. (3) Full admin-feature audit across all 13 admin.html sidebar domains found one genuine dead surface: the 'documents' domain (public/js/admin/primer-admin.js) wrote to the archive_documents 'primer' type but had zero remaining consumer (the player-facing Primer tab it fed was deleted in #1135; the primer players actually read is an unrelated static page). Removed the sidebar domain, the panel, and the now-unreachable primer-type branches in server/routes/archive-documents.js (dossier/history_submission/downtime_response types on that route untouched). PR #1150, merged to main 000e2aec, dev synced to 493cba81. Changed-area regression (api-archive-documents.test.js) 21/21, confirmed no Playwright spec covers the removed admin surface. (4) Created this repo's first .claude/session-wrap.md playbook (none existed before this session). Full detail in this session's own conversation record, no dedicated story file - this was audit/cleanup work, not a BMAD story. Prior entry follows.)" All three stories done: oaq.1 (data-lock), oaq.2 (pending Status Actions backend, internal 3-layer review), oaq.3 (ST approval-queue tab, external Codex review). oaq.3's review found and fixed a real, previously-undetected crash: a true concurrent accept-vs-accept race on ONE pending record hit an uncaught 500 via the same stale issue-1143 office_actions unique index oaq.2's own review believed it had fully closed - that fix only covered two separate pending records racing, not two requests racing the same record. Fixed by reordering the accept transaction so the pending-record resolve gate runs before the log insert. Also patched a dev-role PII leak (raw character/ST names shown unredacted in the new tab). Committed locally (c19f2606 on ms/oaq-2-pending-status-actions-accept-decline), not pushed