feat(office-tab): oxp-6 purchase and affordability markers
Adds a per-seat office-XP balance and per-dot affordability/rank-order
reasons to the Office tab, and swaps hand-built Unicode dots for the
app's standard CSS dot markup. Closes oxp-5's own hard dependency:
officeXpSpentForCategory now folds manoeuvre_xp_destroyed into spend,
so a handover's destroyed XP no longer silently reappears as a refund
the moment a balance renders.

External Codex review found a real information-disclosure bug: an
unconfirmed own-office view (a multi-seat category with no holder
match) leaked that fallback seat's real balance and affordability
reasons as if they were the viewer's own. Fixed by requiring
outcome.confirmed alongside isOwnOffice, mirroring the pre-existing
manoeuvre-list muting guard that already got this right. Also fixed:
a shared Promise.all had coupled the two purchase sections' failure
states, so one endpoint failing blanked both instead of failing
independently. Full triage in the story's Senior Developer Review
section and code-review/oxp-6-codex-findings.md. Re-verified:
