 163: ### DBO-3 — XP-spend merit picker: the `standing` filter has never fired
 164: 
 165: `getItemsForCategory('merit')` skips `sub_category === 'standing'`, but Mystery Cult Initiation and
 166: Professional Training carry `special: 'standing'` with `sub_category: null`. So the filter has
 167: **never** excluded the two merits its own comment names, and excludes `Confessor`/`Pledged` instead.
 168: 
 169: Live defect in the app players use. Same class as a naming mismatch the Wiki found on its own side
 170: (`"Theban Sorcery"` vs the `"Theban"` sheet key). Note DBO-1 may change what `special` is allowed to
 171: be, so sequence this after it or design the fix to survive either outcome.
 172: 
 173: ### DBO-4 — Office collections: absent, empty, and a route pointing at nothing — RESOLVED 2026-08-14
 174: 
 175: - **`office_manoeuvre_ranks` does not exist in live Atlas.** Not empty — absent. The route at
 176:   `server/routes/office-manoeuvre-rank.js:7` refers to it.
 177: - **`office_actions`** holds 0 documents; **`office_merit_dots`** holds 2.
 178: 
 179: Relevant to the OXP epic: code renders differently against dev fixtures than against production.
 180: Decide per surface whether "renders empty" is an intended quiet failure or a defect, and make it
 181: explicit rather than a discovery at the table.
 182: 
 183: **RESOLVED, dev-storied 2026-08-14 — this section's own "not yet merged" premise was stale.**
 184: `git log origin/main` (checked at dev time) shows `oxp-1` through `oxp-6` and `oxp-11` already merged
 185: (oxp-5 via PR #1165, merge commit `1063787b`) — this repo's own `epic-oxp` sprint-status row was
 186: itself stale on the same point. Findings, all confirmed against live `tm_suite` (read-only queries):
 187: 
 188: - **`office_manoeuvre_ranks` and `office_merit_dots`'s "no document = 0" convention is deliberate**,
 189:   not a gap — confirmed by reading every writer (both `PUT` routes' `upsert: true`, the one reset path
 190:   `resetManoeuvreRank` in `server/routes/office-seats.js:501-544`'s explicit `upsert: false`, with an
 191:   inline comment naming this exact convention). Not a defect.
 192: - **`office_actions` genuinely holds 0 documents because no office action has ever been approved
 193:   through the pipeline** — confirmed by reading the full `POST`/`accept`/`decline` write paths
 194:   (transactional, no silent-failure branch; any non-`RouteResponse` error re-throws as a 500 rather
 195:   than being swallowed). Not a defect.
 196: - **The "renders differently against dev fixtures than production" claim is answered, and it is a
 197:   real, live, currently-open hazard**: `office_merit_dots` holds 2 REAL pre-migration documents still
 198:   keyed by office category (`"Enforcer"`, `"Head of State"`), not by seat. `server/scripts/migrate-
 199:   office-purchases-to-seats.mjs` (built and reviewed alongside oxp-11, dry-run default) has not been
 200:   run against live `tm_suite` — until it is, the current seat-keyed code cannot see either document
