 202:   `{"Safe Place": 0}`, so nothing of real value is at stake *today* — but the migration script's own
 203:   header names a compounding hazard: an ST setting a merit dot on either seat before the migration
 204:   runs creates a fresh seat-keyed document, after which the migration will treat the old category-
 205:   keyed one as already-migrated and leave it permanently orphaned. **Running `--apply` is Angelus's
 206:   action, not an agent's** (same standing convention as DBO-1's own cleanup script) — flagged here,
 207:   in `specs/reference-data-ssot.md`'s new Office section, and in `deferred-work.md` for visibility
